INT. BAKERY DELIVERY TRUCK - CARGO AREA - PRE-DAWN

Steel racks of bread trays. Flour hangs in the air. A single dome light. The truck rocks gently over a country road.

Three crew members and a stranger sit among the loaves.

MARISOL "MARI" BENNETT-OKORO (30s, flour-dusted overalls, driver's cap) kneels in the aisle with a wrench. HECTOR DELACROIX-ASANTE (40s, forearms like hams, a neat moustache) sorts baguettes into bags. PRIYA RAMASWAMY-LINDQVIST (20s, hairnet, earbuds) counts a stack of invoices. And in the corner, wedged between two racks with a bakery apron over his suit, sits THE STRANGER (50s, polished shoes, a briefcase handcuffed to his wrist).

MARI
Radio check.

PRIYA
(into collar)
One.

HECTOR
Two.

MARI
Three. Stranger?

THE STRANGER
I'm not on the radio.

MARI
You're on now.

THE STRANGER
I'm a delivery.

HECTOR
Pastry delivery.

THE STRANGER
(wearily)
Very funny.

He tugs at the handcuff. It doesn't give. Priya pulls out an earbud.

PRIYA
How long do we hold him?

MARI
Until the bank opens.

PRIYA
That's four hours.

MARI
So we'll have fresh bread.

Hector chuckles. The truck turns onto gravel. Loaves shift. The stranger lowers his head.

THE STRANGER
You know I can pay.

HECTOR
Everybody can pay.

THE STRANGER
Double what they're giving you.

MARI
That's what they all say.

PRIYA
(low, to Mari)
Is it a lot?

MARI
(low)
Not enough.

Hector pushes aside a tray to reach the stranger's briefcase. The man jerks it away. Hector slaps the man's wrist, once, and the case springs open. Inside, a silver dossier. Hector flips it open.

HECTOR
Mari.

MARI
What.

HECTOR
His name is Julian Ashworth-Mbeki.

Marisol freezes. Priya drops her invoices. The stranger lifts his chin. His face, in the dome light, is perfectly composed.

JULIAN
That is my name.

MARI
(softly)
You're the auditor.

JULIAN
I am.

MARI
Hector, we grabbed the wrong man.

HECTOR
We grabbed the right man.

PRIYA
He's the auditor!

HECTOR
The auditor with the files.

They look at each other. Julian smiles. The truck bounces over a pothole and a tray of croissants slides off its rack and scatters across the floor.

JULIAN
Well. Shall we eat?
